      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Motion: read a clip into its depth, its targets' mask and its first frame",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Motion: read a clip into its depth, its targets' mask and its first frame\n\nReads up to 10 seconds of a clip at a short side of at most 768 px. Depth Anything 3 Mono-Large makes its depth video, SAM 3.1 tracks one object for each of up to 3 things named by text into one mask video, and the first frame is saved. The three guide the LTX 2.5 render of Motion's Change a clip.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Your clip, node 1. The first 10 seconds are read.\n- What to find, node 21: up to 3 short descriptions of things in the clip, separated by commas, such as `the man in the grey coat, the bottle in his hand`. Each finds one thing.\n- The most objects to track, node 22: one per thing you named, so a person beside them stays out of the mask.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- The depth video, node 13: Depth Anything 3 Mono-Large reads each frame, near is white and far is black.\n- The mask video, node 28: SAM 3.1 tracks each thing you named through the clip. The mask is white on them and black elsewhere, with hard edges. The render grows and feathers it.\n- The first frame, node 31.\n\nAll three keep the clip's frame rate, with the short side at most 768 px.\n\n## Models\n\n- [da3mono_large.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/depth-anything/DA3MONO-LARGE): Depth Anything 3 Mono-Large, by ByteDance Seed, [Apache 2.0](https://huggingface.co/depth-anything/DA3MONO-LARGE). It loads through [ComfyUI-DepthAnythingV3](https://github.com/PozzettiAndrea/ComfyUI-DepthAnythingV3), MIT, at commit `20ef6c8ccf8d57a0ad6f6fa7031739eb8489f2a4`.\n- [sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam3.1): SAM 3.1, by Meta, under the SAM License in `sam-license.txt`. Its nodes are ComfyUI core.\n\nRosesfield ships no weights. Each loader lists its file with a download link.\n\nPart of [Rosesfield](https://github.com/rossaai/rosesfield), MIT."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
  ],
